<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Indonesian National Armed Forces</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1945–</span> · Also known as Tentara Nasional Indonesia, TNI</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Indonesian National Armed Forces (Tentara Nasional <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>, TNI) are the army, navy and air force of Indonesia. They grew out of the militias and security forces formed in 1945 to fight the returning <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a>, and 5 October is kept as Armed Forces Day. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suharto">Suharto</a>'s New Order the doctrine of dual function gave officers a role in government, which was dismantled after 1998, when the police were also separated from the military.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/indonesian-national-armed-forces.jpg" alt="Indonesian National Armed Forces" width="320" height="301" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tentara Nasional Indonesia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Insignia_of_the_Indonesian_National_Armed_Forces.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
